oQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"1Tf1W0Abh0-JyvhHVb_3VA","review_id":"2ZpMy2NOv8FEpwSnwurzxg","date":"2011-04-06T13:17:50","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9529772996902466,"text_excerpt":"Pralines by Jean was the first taste of New Orleans pralines during my visit to NOLA. It was freakin delicious! So buttery and sweet with fresh pecans. Yummie! And for $2 each, they are totally affordable. Definitely a great local shop worth supporting! Thanks! By the way, they serve cupcakes here too. =)"},{"business_id":"1Tf1W0Abh0-JyvhHVb_3VA","review_id":"C-Wh9iO853fFvySxt4iUCw","date":"2013-08-14T19:07:42","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9331864714622498,"text_excerpt":"I am not a fan of pralines (gasp!), so I can't really comment on them. However, I DO like the cupcakes - and these are some FANCY cupcakes! The Vanilla Rum and Butter Pecan are my favorite :) The lady (forgot her name) was very sweet and helpful. She even shared some great Resaturant ideas for us to visit during our stay in NOLA. This is my 2nd time there (from Dallas). I WILL RETURN :)"},{"business_id":"1Tf1W0Abh0-JyvhHVb_3VA","review_id":"2KcUFFi28FXZlWACXMbQig","date":"2014-02-19T01:13:15","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9293176531791687,"text_excerpt":"It's not just pralines... but it could be, because these sugary/nutty/creamy delights are good enough to stand on their own! Whenever I have visitors in town seeking the classic NOLA confection, I bring them to Jean's. Unlike some of the shops in the Quarter, Jean makes her pralines on the premises. That is, she doesn't get them from some factory where they grind 'em out by the hundreds (and put in nasty extra cheapo ingredients). And you can totally notice the difference that a little bit of love and care for the final product makes! She sources all of the ingredients locally. Jean is a saint of sweets! Besides pralines, however, there's also a bunch of fun NOLA souvenirs that you can ad..."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
